\paragraph{Contributions.}
On FOLIO with Qwen3, across 6 reward conditions, 5 seeds, 2 logic types, 2 model scales, and up to 1000 steps:
(\textbf{C1}) We empirically demonstrate ISR as a diagnostic for GRPO reward hacking, revealing a 99.5\% collapse trajectory invisible to prove rate, with an SFT control consistent with RL-specific failure (\S\ref{sec:diagnostic});
(\textbf{C2}) an empirical characterization of Goodhart collapse dynamics under LOO-based rewards, including seed-dependent divergence, dose-varying patterns across four $\beta$ levels, cross-logic mode divergence, and a hacking taxonomy of eight automated-classifier modes plus one manual-audit mode (H9) spanning two logic types and two model scales (\S\ref{sec:goodhart}--\ref{sec:taxonomy});
